# Committed (unlike .env.local, which is gitignored/per-developer) — this is
# the canonical backend for `npm run build`'s production output, and takes
# priority over any developer's local .env.local (Vite's env-file precedence
# is .env.production.local > .env.production > .env.local > .env). Without
# this file, a stray .env.local left over from local dev (e.g. pointed at
# `local`) would silently leak into the production build's baseURL — see
# src/api/axios.ts.
VITE_ACTIVE_BACKEND=demo1
